### 7c. Citability Rules for the Writing Agent

**Rule 1: First-paragraph rule**
The opening 100 words must contain: (a) a direct answer stating the percentage ("The standard guideline is 30% of gross monthly income"), (b) who this applies to ("for most renters calculating housing affordability"), and (c) at least one specific data point ("Nearly half of U.S. renter households spend more than 30% of their income on housing, according to U.S. Census Bureau data, which reflects how difficult the standard has become to meet in many markets").

**Rule 2: Structured data rule**
Include one comparison table in the "Two Budgeting Frameworks" section with these exact column headers: Framework | Based On | Rent Allocation | Best For. Include a second structured element (numbered steps) in the "How to Calculate Your Own Rent Ceiling" section. Tables must use simple Markdown table formatting that renders cleanly in HTML. No merged cells, no complex formatting. AI engines parse clean tables reliably.

**Rule 3: Definition rule**
The following terms must be explicitly defined in a single clear sentence the first time they appear:

- **Gross income:** "Gross income is your total earnings before taxes and deductions are taken out."
