- **Rent-to-income ratio:** "The rent-to-income ratio is the percentage of your gross monthly income that goes toward monthly rent, calculated by dividing monthly rent by gross monthly income and multiplying by 100."
- **3x rent rule:** "The 3x rent rule is a landlord screening standard requiring an applicant's gross monthly income to be at least three times the monthly rent."

